{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "gr-comparing",
  "connector": "-er / -est",
  "gloss": "比べる",
  "title": "bigger, the biggest — 比べる（比較級・最上級）",
  "pattern": "-er than … ／ more … than … ／ the -est ／ the most …",
  "explanation": "2つを比べる時は、短い形容詞に -er をつけて than を続けます：Wellington is windier than Auckland.長い形容詞は more：more expensive than。「いちばん」は the -est か the most：the biggest、the most beautiful。good → better → best、bad → worse → worst は形が変わります。",
  "natural": "選ぶ時に：Which one is cheaper?（どっちが安い？）、This is the best pie I’ve ever had!（今まで食べた中でいちばんおいしいパイ！）",
  "stiff": "more と -er を両方つけないこと：more cheaper はまちがいで、cheaper。",
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "gx-comparing-1",
      "english": "Wellington is windier than Auckland.",
      "japanese": "ウェリントンはオークランドより風が強いです。",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "t": "Wellington is "
        },
        {
